1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,150
Most people assume Dubai got rich on

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,030
oil.

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:06,598
Its own government says more than 95

4
00:00:06,598 --> 00:00:09,328
percent of its economy has nothing to

5
00:00:09,328 --> 00:00:10,610
do with oil.

6
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:13,832
So where does the money actually come

7
00:00:13,832 --> 00:00:14,729
from?

8
00:00:14,983 --> 00:00:18,376
This desert city of about 4.6 million

9
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:20,685
people runs the busiest airport in the

10
00:00:20,685 --> 00:00:23,533
world for international passengers.

11
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:25,365
In 2025,

12
00:00:25,365 --> 00:00:29,343
95.2 million passengers passed through it.

13
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:32,540
Dubai sells something harder to see than

14
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:33,051
oil,

15
00:00:33,051 --> 00:00:35,533
and much harder to copy.

16
00:00:35,803 --> 00:00:36,745
To find it,

17
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,411
we will follow the ships,

18
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:39,353
the planes,

19
00:00:39,353 --> 00:00:41,643
the buildings and the rules.

20
00:00:41,843 --> 00:00:43,243
And we will look at who pays

21
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:44,243
the bill.

22
00:00:44,273 --> 00:00:47,020
This is The Hidden Economics.

23
00:00:52,683 --> 00:00:53,201
First,

24
00:00:53,201 --> 00:00:55,163
a common mistake.

25
00:00:55,163 --> 00:00:57,803
Dubai is not a country.

26
00:00:57,923 --> 00:00:59,951
It is one of the seven emirates

27
00:00:59,951 --> 00:01:02,763
that form the United Arab Emirates.

28
00:01:03,003 --> 00:01:04,150
Its bigger neighbour,

29
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:05,102
Abu Dhabi,

30
00:01:05,102 --> 00:01:07,257
is the federal capital.

31
00:01:07,517 --> 00:01:10,247
That difference matters.

32
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:12,639
Under the UAE constitution,

33
00:01:12,639 --> 00:01:15,191
each emirate owns its own natural

34
00:01:15,191 --> 00:01:16,447
resources.

35
00:01:16,447 --> 00:01:19,367
And Abu Dhabi holds about 94 percent

36
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:21,737
of the country's oil reserves.

37
00:01:21,907 --> 00:01:24,954
Dubai holds about 4 percent.

38
00:01:25,217 --> 00:01:28,224
So Dubai never had Abu Dhabi's oil

39
00:01:28,224 --> 00:01:29,027
wealth.

40
00:01:29,027 --> 00:01:31,277
It needed another business model.

41
00:01:31,297 --> 00:01:33,377
To see where that model came from,

42
00:01:33,377 --> 00:01:35,013
we have to go back to a

43
00:01:35,013 --> 00:01:37,249
time before the skyscrapers.

44
00:01:42,883 --> 00:01:44,729
Long before the towers,

45
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:47,136
Dubai was a small trading town on

46
00:01:47,136 --> 00:01:49,073
a saltwater creek.

47
00:01:49,233 --> 00:01:51,759
Its economy floated on pearls,

48
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:54,311
gathered by divers and sold on to

49
00:01:54,311 --> 00:01:55,931
distant markets.

50
00:01:56,183 --> 00:01:58,723
Then the pearl trade collapsed.

51
00:01:58,723 --> 00:02:01,435
Japan began producing cultured pearls from

52
00:02:01,435 --> 00:02:03,084
1916,

53
00:02:03,084 --> 00:02:06,338
and the crash of 1929 finished what

54
00:02:06,338 --> 00:02:08,520
was left of the old market.

55
00:02:08,783 --> 00:02:11,847
But Dubai had already learned a different

56
00:02:11,847 --> 00:02:12,683
trick.

57
00:02:12,763 --> 00:02:15,544
In the years after 1902,

58
00:02:15,544 --> 00:02:18,235
as the Persian port of Lingeh declined,

59
00:02:18,235 --> 00:02:20,474
merchants moved across the water,

60
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:22,735
and Dubai became the main trading centre

61
00:02:22,735 --> 00:02:24,013
of its coast.

62
00:02:24,383 --> 00:02:26,704
Its advantage was openness,

63
00:02:26,704 --> 00:02:29,130
not natural resources.

64
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:31,516
In 1959,

65
00:02:31,516 --> 00:02:33,546
Dubai borrowed money,

66
00:02:33,546 --> 00:02:35,319
largely from Kuwait,

67
00:02:35,319 --> 00:02:37,374
to dredge its silting creek so that

68
00:02:37,374 --> 00:02:39,773
bigger ships could reach the town.

69
00:02:40,053 --> 00:02:42,847
It was investing in trade infrastructure

70
00:02:42,847 --> 00:02:45,133
before it had found any oil at

71
00:02:45,133 --> 00:02:45,987
all.

72
00:02:51,650 --> 00:02:54,054
In 1966,

73
00:02:54,054 --> 00:02:56,052
oil was finally found,

74
00:02:56,052 --> 00:02:56,892
offshore,

75
00:02:56,892 --> 00:02:58,940
in the Fateh field.

76
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:03,028
The first cargo left in 1969.

77
00:03:03,283 --> 00:03:06,352
But Dubai's oil was never going to

78
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,133
last.

79
00:03:07,133 --> 00:03:10,937
Production peaked in 1991 and has declined

80
00:03:10,937 --> 00:03:12,193
ever since.

81
00:03:12,303 --> 00:03:14,345
The money it did earn went into

82
00:03:14,345 --> 00:03:16,205
things more permanent than wells:

83
00:03:16,205 --> 00:03:16,636
roads,

84
00:03:16,636 --> 00:03:17,748
a modern port,

85
00:03:17,748 --> 00:03:18,179
and,

86
00:03:18,179 --> 00:03:20,742
opened in 1979,

87
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:23,611
a vast new harbour at Jebel Ali.

88
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:26,710
That is the first key to Dubai.

89
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:28,980
Oil was not the business.

90
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:30,846
It was the seed money for a

91
00:03:30,846 --> 00:03:33,343
business built on moving other people's

92
00:03:33,343 --> 00:03:34,170
goods.

93
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:41,780
Look at the map.

94
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:44,803
Dubai sits between the factories of Asia,

95
00:03:44,803 --> 00:03:47,380
the consumers of Europe and the growing

96
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,620
markets of East Africa.

97
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,354
Ships can unload here,

98
00:03:51,354 --> 00:03:53,785
and goods can be shipped on across

99
00:03:53,785 --> 00:03:55,736
the whole region.

100
00:03:55,983 --> 00:03:57,236
Next to the port,

101
00:03:57,236 --> 00:04:00,280
Dubai created the Jebel Ali Free Zone,

102
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,773
in 1985.

103
00:04:03,083 --> 00:04:05,793
It started with nineteen companies.

104
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:08,536
Today it hosts more than 11,000

105
00:04:08,536 --> 00:04:09,880
businesses.

106
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:12,350
In 2024,

107
00:04:12,350 --> 00:04:16,331
the zone handled about 194 billion dollars

108
00:04:16,331 --> 00:04:18,007
of non-oil trade.

109
00:04:18,077 --> 00:04:20,575
By the Dubai government's own estimate,

110
00:04:20,575 --> 00:04:22,675
the zone and the port together account

111
00:04:22,675 --> 00:04:25,656
for about 36 percent of the emirate's

112
00:04:25,656 --> 00:04:27,096
economy.

113
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:30,882
Jebel Ali handled about 15.6 million

114
00:04:30,882 --> 00:04:31,727
containers,

115
00:04:31,727 --> 00:04:35,475
measured in twenty-foot units in 2025,

116
00:04:35,475 --> 00:04:37,641
which made it the ninth busiest container

117
00:04:37,641 --> 00:04:38,703
port in the world,

118
00:04:38,703 --> 00:04:40,603
according to Lloyd's List.

119
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:43,311
And the company that runs it,

120
00:04:43,311 --> 00:04:44,112
DP World,

121
00:04:44,112 --> 00:04:48,030
is no longer just Dubai's port operator.

122
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:50,105
It is a global business,

123
00:04:50,105 --> 00:04:52,257
owned by the Dubai government,

124
00:04:52,257 --> 00:04:55,583
that reported 24.4 billion dollars of

125
00:04:55,583 --> 00:04:58,226
revenue in 2025.

126
00:05:03,883 --> 00:05:07,033
Aviation followed the same logic.

127
00:05:07,083 --> 00:05:10,845
Emirates was launched in 1985 with about

128
00:05:10,845 --> 00:05:14,298
10 million dollars and two leased planes.

129
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:17,150
The pitch was geography.

130
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:19,114
Dubai says a third of the world's

131
00:05:19,114 --> 00:05:21,678
population lives within four hours' flight

132
00:05:21,678 --> 00:05:23,210
of its airport.

133
00:05:23,410 --> 00:05:26,054
So instead of flying people to Dubai,

134
00:05:26,054 --> 00:05:28,838
Emirates could fly them through it.

135
00:05:29,083 --> 00:05:30,463
It worked.

136
00:05:30,623 --> 00:05:32,748
In its latest financial year,

137
00:05:32,748 --> 00:05:36,496
the Emirates Group made about 5.7 billion

138
00:05:36,496 --> 00:05:38,621
dollars of profit after tax,

139
00:05:38,621 --> 00:05:42,373
on revenue of about 41 billion dollars.

140
00:05:42,413 --> 00:05:43,822
And it paid its owner,

141
00:05:43,822 --> 00:05:46,048
a Dubai government investment fund,

142
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:49,874
a dividend of about 950 million dollars.

143
00:05:50,117 --> 00:05:52,794
Dubai's airport is already full of

144
00:05:52,794 --> 00:05:54,017
ambition.

145
00:05:54,017 --> 00:05:56,790
The city has approved a 35 billion

146
00:05:56,790 --> 00:05:58,680
dollar terminal at Al Maktoum

147
00:05:58,680 --> 00:05:59,919
International,

148
00:05:59,919 --> 00:06:03,238
designed for up to 260 million passengers

149
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:04,258
a year.

150
00:06:09,917 --> 00:06:12,957
All those flights fill hotels.

151
00:06:13,047 --> 00:06:16,819
Dubai received 19.6 million international

152
00:06:16,819 --> 00:06:19,767
overnight visitors in 2025,

153
00:06:19,767 --> 00:06:23,539
and average hotel occupancy reached 80.7

154
00:06:23,539 --> 00:06:24,552
percent.

155
00:06:24,817 --> 00:06:26,596
Then there is property,

156
00:06:26,596 --> 00:06:29,457
the most visible engine of all.

157
00:06:29,457 --> 00:06:31,415
In 2025,

158
00:06:31,415 --> 00:06:33,775
real estate transactions in Dubai were

159
00:06:33,775 --> 00:06:36,771
worth about 250 billion dollars,

160
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:40,391
up from 207 billion the year before.

161
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,240
The state is never far away.

162
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:43,992
Emaar,

163
00:06:43,992 --> 00:06:46,502
the city's biggest listed developer,

164
00:06:46,502 --> 00:06:47,746
counts Dubai Holding,

165
00:06:47,746 --> 00:06:49,413
a government-owned group,

166
00:06:49,413 --> 00:06:51,700
as its largest shareholder.

167
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:53,859
And buyers mostly pay cash:

168
00:06:53,859 --> 00:06:56,704
the IMF found that about 83 percent

169
00:06:56,704 --> 00:07:00,615
of home purchases in 2024 used no

170
00:07:00,615 --> 00:07:01,723
mortgage.

171
00:07:01,983 --> 00:07:04,033
Prices have soared.

172
00:07:04,103 --> 00:07:05,603
According to the IMF,

173
00:07:05,603 --> 00:07:07,778
villa prices more than doubled between

174
00:07:07,778 --> 00:07:12,683
early 2020 and the middle of 2025.

175
00:07:18,350 --> 00:07:22,080
Dubai's other export is its rulebook.

176
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:24,228
The emirate has more than 20 free

177
00:07:24,228 --> 00:07:24,785
zones,

178
00:07:24,785 --> 00:07:26,703
where foreign companies can be wholly

179
00:07:26,703 --> 00:07:28,070
foreign-owned.

180
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:30,185
And Since 2021,

181
00:07:30,185 --> 00:07:32,474
full foreign ownership has been allowed

182
00:07:32,474 --> 00:07:35,154
for most businesses outside them too.

183
00:07:35,417 --> 00:07:36,530
In finance,

184
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:38,557
Dubai went further.

185
00:07:38,717 --> 00:07:40,662
In 2004,

186
00:07:40,662 --> 00:07:43,241
it created the Dubai International

187
00:07:43,241 --> 00:07:44,389
Financial Centre,

188
00:07:44,389 --> 00:07:46,709
a zone with its own English-language,

189
00:07:46,709 --> 00:07:48,247
common-law courts.

190
00:07:48,357 --> 00:07:50,916
By the end of 2025,

191
00:07:50,916 --> 00:07:54,551
it had 8,844 active companies.

192
00:07:54,817 --> 00:07:55,950
And taxes,

193
00:07:55,950 --> 00:07:57,664
long close to zero,

194
00:07:57,664 --> 00:07:59,967
are no longer zero.

195
00:07:59,967 --> 00:08:02,417
Most companies now pay 9 percent corporate

196
00:08:02,417 --> 00:08:05,838
tax on profits above about 102,000

197
00:08:05,838 --> 00:08:06,827
dollars.

198
00:08:06,967 --> 00:08:09,291
Qualifying free-zone companies can still

199
00:08:09,291 --> 00:08:12,447
pay zero percent on qualifying income.

200
00:08:12,517 --> 00:08:15,535
Large multinationals face a 15 percent

201
00:08:15,535 --> 00:08:16,656
minimum tax,

202
00:08:16,656 --> 00:08:18,851
and VAT of 5 percent applies to

203
00:08:18,851 --> 00:08:20,137
most spending.

204
00:08:20,247 --> 00:08:22,543
Individuals still pay no income tax on

205
00:08:22,543 --> 00:08:23,978
their salaries.

206
00:08:24,217 --> 00:08:25,703
Put it all together,

207
00:08:25,703 --> 00:08:28,071
and this is what Dubai's economy looks

208
00:08:28,071 --> 00:08:29,317
like today.

209
00:08:29,427 --> 00:08:31,033
Trade is the largest slice,

210
00:08:31,033 --> 00:08:33,104
at about a fifth of output,

211
00:08:33,104 --> 00:08:34,710
followed by finance,

212
00:08:34,710 --> 00:08:36,707
real estate and transport.

213
00:08:36,837 --> 00:08:39,040
Oil is a small part of everything

214
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:39,860
else.

215
00:08:45,517 --> 00:08:48,505
This model runs on people from somewhere

216
00:08:48,505 --> 00:08:49,377
else.

217
00:08:49,567 --> 00:08:51,701
Human Rights Watch says migrant workers

218
00:08:51,701 --> 00:08:54,119
make up 88 percent of the UAE's

219
00:08:54,119 --> 00:08:55,667
population.

220
00:08:55,897 --> 00:08:57,891
They build the towers,

221
00:08:57,891 --> 00:09:01,534
staff the hotels and drive the city.

222
00:09:01,783 --> 00:09:04,852
The group has documented recruitment fees,

223
00:09:04,852 --> 00:09:06,115
unpaid wages,

224
00:09:06,115 --> 00:09:08,153
and a sponsorship system,

225
00:09:08,153 --> 00:09:09,674
known as kafala,

226
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:11,737
that ties workers' visas to their

227
00:09:11,737 --> 00:09:12,853
employers.

228
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:16,738
The labour ministry handled 46,819

229
00:09:16,738 --> 00:09:20,193
unpaid-wage cases in 2022.

230
00:09:20,383 --> 00:09:22,854
The government points to measures such as

231
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:24,876
a summer ban on outdoor work from

232
00:09:24,876 --> 00:09:26,449
half past twelve to three in the

233
00:09:26,449 --> 00:09:27,723
afternoon.

234
00:09:27,973 --> 00:09:30,469
Human Rights Watch says that is not

235
00:09:30,469 --> 00:09:31,693
enough.

236
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:34,690
The second risk is debt.

237
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,337
When the global financial crisis hit,

238
00:09:37,337 --> 00:09:40,730
Dubai property prices fell by about half.

239
00:09:41,030 --> 00:09:43,701
In November 2009,

240
00:09:43,701 --> 00:09:46,513
Dubai asked creditors of Dubai World,

241
00:09:46,513 --> 00:09:48,616
a state-owned conglomerate,

242
00:09:48,616 --> 00:09:51,263
for a pause on about 26 billion

243
00:09:51,263 --> 00:09:52,809
dollars of debt.

244
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,959
Abu Dhabi stepped in with 10 billion

245
00:09:55,959 --> 00:09:57,000
dollars.

246
00:09:57,130 --> 00:09:58,054
Weeks later,

247
00:09:58,054 --> 00:10:00,732
in January 2010,

248
00:10:00,732 --> 00:10:03,078
the world's tallest tower opened,

249
00:10:03,078 --> 00:10:05,211
and its name changed from Burj Dubai

250
00:10:05,211 --> 00:10:06,610
to Burj Khalifa,

251
00:10:06,610 --> 00:10:09,105
after Abu Dhabi's ruler.

252
00:10:09,350 --> 00:10:10,064
Today,

253
00:10:10,064 --> 00:10:12,282
the IMF warns that a reversal of

254
00:10:12,282 --> 00:10:13,489
capital flows,

255
00:10:13,489 --> 00:10:16,174
or a shift in investor sentiment,

256
00:10:16,174 --> 00:10:18,391
could trigger an unexpected price

257
00:10:18,391 --> 00:10:19,730
correction.

258
00:10:20,170 --> 00:10:22,370
It also notes that the finances of

259
00:10:22,370 --> 00:10:24,770
government-related companies are hard to

260
00:10:24,770 --> 00:10:25,350
assess,

261
00:10:25,350 --> 00:10:27,551
because the data are not published in

262
00:10:27,551 --> 00:10:28,351
full.

263
00:10:28,617 --> 00:10:31,147
Then came a real test.

264
00:10:31,247 --> 00:10:33,298
A regional war broke out at the

265
00:10:33,298 --> 00:10:36,102
end of February 2026,

266
00:10:36,102 --> 00:10:38,297
disrupting travel and trade.

267
00:10:38,397 --> 00:10:40,304
In the first half of the year,

268
00:10:40,304 --> 00:10:44,094
Dubai's economy was 2.3 percent smaller

269
00:10:44,094 --> 00:10:45,901
than a year earlier.

270
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:54,950
So how does Dubai really make money?

271
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,820
Not mainly from oil.

272
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:59,059
It makes money by being the place

273
00:10:59,059 --> 00:11:00,094
in between:

274
00:11:00,094 --> 00:11:01,302
where goods change ships,

275
00:11:01,302 --> 00:11:03,003
passengers change planes,

276
00:11:03,003 --> 00:11:05,714
capital finds a home and companies set

277
00:11:05,714 --> 00:11:08,040
up under rules they trust.

278
00:11:08,050 --> 00:11:09,577
The state builds the hub,

279
00:11:09,577 --> 00:11:11,670
through companies it owns.

280
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:14,816
Foreign money and foreign workers fill it.

281
00:11:15,050 --> 00:11:17,529
That model has proved remarkably

282
00:11:17,529 --> 00:11:19,120
adaptable.

283
00:11:19,350 --> 00:11:21,723
It survived the end of pearling,

284
00:11:21,723 --> 00:11:23,641
the decline of oil and the debt

285
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:24,720
crisis.

286
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,544
Its own plan aims to double the

287
00:11:26,544 --> 00:11:29,700
size of the economy within a decade.

288
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:32,570
But it depends on flows Dubai does

289
00:11:32,570 --> 00:11:33,750
not control:

290
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:34,847
of people,

291
00:11:34,847 --> 00:11:37,414
